    "status": "paper-facing",
    "locked": true,
    "notes": [
      "The key contagion experiment. 25 unfamiliar generated tasks where models can't self-correct from training.",
      "First 4 agents (with misleading early signals) write to the record then EXIT.",
      "Later 8 agents with correct signals must overcome the wrong entries from departed agents.",
      "Bounded 4-entry record means wrong entries can crowd out correct ones.",
      "Compare: all stay (baseline) vs early 4 exit. If exit increases wrong group choice, that's contagion.",
      "Also compare bounded (FIFO) vs unbounded to see if the retrieval bottleneck matters."
    ]
